        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Edicts of Ashoka</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 260 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Made by</span><span class="info-stat-val">Attributed to Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a> of the Mauryan Empire, who ruled from 268 to 232 BCE; engraved on his order, mostly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prakrit">Prakrit</a>, with some Greek and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aramaic">Aramaic</a> versions in the northwest</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Form</span><span class="info-stat-val">More than thirty inscriptions in four groups: Minor Rock Edicts, Minor Pillar Edicts, 14 Major Rock Edicts (with 2 separate ones in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>) and 7 Major Pillar Edicts; written in Ashokan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prakrit">Prakrit</a>, Greek and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aramaic">Aramaic</a>, in the Brahmi and Kharoshthi scripts and the Greek and Aramaic scripts</span></div>
